Fuzix for the Commodore Amiga
=============================

First target: a stock A1200 (68EC020, 2MB chip RAM, AGA, Gayle IDE,
Kickstart 3.1). Fast RAM is used when exec reports it. Tested in FS-UAE
only so far.

Booting
-------
Two floppies are built:

  fuzix.adf          boot floppy; the root file system is on the IDE disk
  fuzix-floppy.adf   the whole system on one floppy (no hard disk needed):
                     bootblock with an MBR partition table, the kernel,
                     and a 780K Fuzix file system from sector 200 with the
                     small tool set (Standalone/filesystem-src/
                     fuzix-amigafloppy.pkg)

If the boot floppy has a Fuzix partition it is the root (hda1); otherwise
the root is the first IDE disk's first partition (hdb1 while a disk is in
the drive, hda1 if not).

The kernel boots from a floppy. The bootblock
(bootblock.S) reads the kernel through trackdisk, notes chip and fast RAM
from exec's memory list, stops the drive motor, shuts the OS down,
copies the kernel to $400 and jumps to it. The root file system is the
first partition of the IDE disk (Images/amiga/disk.img, MBR partitions,
no byte swapping).

  make TARGET=amiga YACC=yacc diskimage     (with m68k-elf-gcc on PATH)

then uae/run.sh boots both in FS-UAE as a stock A1200, headless in cage.
uae/vkey types on the emulated keyboard with real key codes.

What works
----------
- Screen: 640x256 PAL hires, one bitplane, 80x32 text (tty1)
- Keyboard: CIA-A serial, US layout, cursor keys, Ctrl, Shift, Caps
- Serial: Paula on tty2, kernel messages mirrored there at 9600 baud
- Timer: vertical blank, 50Hz
- IDE: Gayle (A1200/A600) through the generic devide driver, PIO
- Floppy: DF0, 880K AmigaDOS-format tracks read and written through
  Paula's disk DMA (devfd.c); a track cache, whole-track writes; the
  motor goes off two seconds after the last use
- Fonts: Fuzix's own 8x8 font, or the Kickstart ROM's Topaz 8 (found in
  any ROM from 1.3 to 3.2); fontprefs picks one and /etc/rc loads it
- Boots to login and a shell in FS-UAE, with and without fast RAM

To do
